# FishMMO — Environment Configuration
#
# This file documents environment variables used for local development.
# Application secrets (gate secret, KEK, connection token HMAC key) are
# stored in the PostgreSQL database and loaded by servers at startup.
# No env vars are needed for application secrets.
#
# Database credentials are the only secrets managed via environment.
# They are resolved by the DatabaseSecrets class from:
#   - FISHMMO_DB_* environment variables (highest priority)
#   - /etc/fishmmo/db-secrets.env (production)
#   - %ProgramData%\FishMMO\db-secrets.env (Windows)
#
# WARNING: Keep real database credentials out of version control.
# Use chmod 600 on any local secrets files.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Database connection (REQUIRED)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are the ONLY secrets that need environment configuration.
# All application keys are loaded from the database at startup.
FISHMMO_DB_HOST=localhost
FISHMMO_DB_PORT=5432
FISHMMO_DB_NAME=fishmmo
FISHMMO_DB_USERNAME=fishmmo
# FISHMMO_DB_PASSWORD=!!!CHANGE_ME!!!

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Environment (optional — defaults to Production)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FISHMMO_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SMTP (optional — for email verification in development)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FISHMMO_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# FISHMMO_SMTP_PORT=587
# FISHMMO_SMTP_USERNAME=
# FISHMMO_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# FISHMMO_SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@example.com
# FISHMMO_SMTP_FROM_NAME=FishMMO
# FISHMMO_SMTP_USE_SSL=true

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Generating Application Keys
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Application keys (gate secret, KEK, connection token HMAC) are
# generated by the FishMMO-Installer and stored in the database:
#
#   Run: fishmmo-installer → Database → Configure Server Keys
#
# Client-side files (ClientApiSecret.generated.cs) are generated
# from within the Unity Editor:
#
#   Unity: FishMMO > Security > Fetch Client Secrets
